{"kind":"note","ts":"2026-05-31T18:21:00Z","note":"Final porter cycle: ROOT-CAUSED both cudatools residual clusters to non-production artifacts; NO source change needed (HEAD stays 74c53d86). Residual A (InterpolationVarShapeWrap.correct_shift) = TEST-FIXTURE use-after-free: async cudaMemcpy2DAsync from a freed per-iteration dstVec; CUDA pageable async is effectively sync, HIP is truly async -> reads freed buffer, garbage in dst padding the kernel does not overwrite. PROVEN via alloc-probe (production hipMemset zeroes full padded buffer), pre/post-kernel probe (padding dirty before kernel, unchanged after), and keep-alive/sync repro (all 21 pass) vs baseline (6-8 fail). Residual B (TypeTraitsMakeTypeVectorTest/3) = char-vs-signed-char identity dictated by upstream HIP_vector_type<char,N> header; forcing signed char rejected as a per-platform hack. cvcuda_test_system stays 0 failures. State porting->ported. 8 new fault classes + changelog entries added to PORTING_GUIDE."}
